$CRM started pulling 45 minutes before close as $MU $SNDK went up.  
$MSFT flash dropped last 10-15 minutes there. again, didnt know rebalancing was today😑

@charliesdollar $MU SanDisk was officially added to the MSCI World Index effective at the Aug. 31 close. MSCI announced that on Aug. 12. That means passive/index-tracking funds had to rebalance into SNDK around the close, which can create the kind of huge closing-volume spike and sudden price jump.  tradingkey.com/analysis/sto...  
SNDK’s late spike was largely mechanical index-flow buying, not a brand-new fundamental memory catalyst.   
For MU, that makes today’s EOD pop less fundamentally bull

